WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:05.360
The Skywalker storyline comes to an end with
Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker, and that’s

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:09.270
too bad because there are plenty of stories
about the most famous family in the galaxy

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:10.180
far, far away.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:14.500
From pirate adventures to clone craziness,
here are the best Skywalker stories we'll

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:15.800
never see in the movies.

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:20.080
Though there were rumors of a turn to the
Dark Side for Luke Skywalker leading up to

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:22.740
The Last Jedi, such a turn never took place.

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:26.640
Luke remained, even in his disillusioned state,
a bastion for good.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:31.320
He got to save the day with his Force projection
duel against Kylo Ren, which allowed the Resistance

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:35.100
fighters to escape and proved that Luke remained
a true hero to his core.

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:39.680
But fans of the Expanded Universe know that
Luke was previously tempted by the Dark Side,

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:42.840
going so far as to become the apprentice to
the Emperor himself.

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:45.480
"I've got a bad feeling about this."

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:49.840
The storyline occurred in one of the first
Expanded Universe stories, the aptly named

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:50.600
Dark Empire.

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:55.720
This 1991 comic book from Dark Horse Comics
takes place just a handful of years after

00:00:55.739 --> 00:00:59.920
Return of the Jedi, and it sees the Emperor
return from his presumed death at the end

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:04.090
of that film, with the explanation being that
he transferred his consciousness to a cloned

00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:05.540
body at the moment of his death.

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:10.060
Luke, shocked to see him alive, agrees to
become his apprentice, with his plan being

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:12.680
to bring down the resurgent Empire from the
inside.

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:15.820
But the Dark Side corrupts Luke, and he loses
sight of his goal.

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:20.100
It takes a lightsaber fight against Leia for
him to snap out of it, and at that point,

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.100
he's finally able to defeat Palpatine.

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:26.100
Dark Luke would've been cool to see on the
big screen, but the window for this story

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:27.320
closed long ago.

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:31.660
In the official Star Wars sequel films, Luke
is not shown to have settled down.

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:35.640
As far as we know, he never had a serious
relationship, never married, and never had

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:36.140
children.

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:40.600
But in the Expanded Universe, Luke did all
of those things with a woman named Mara Jade.

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:45.579
Mara Jade was introduced in the 1991 novel
Heir to the Empire, the first installment

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:48.360
in Timothy Zahn's wildly popular Thrawn trilogy.

00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:53.120
Mara is introduced as a smuggler who was previously
employed as the Emperor's Hand.

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:57.439
She's an extremely skilled user of the Dark
Side of the Force, and prior to the Emperor's

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:00.220
death, Mara was given the command to kill
Luke Skywalker.

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:05.119
She manages to kidnap Luke, but the two subsequently
become stranded in a harsh environment and

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:06.540
must work together to escape.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:11.140
This event starts to bring the two together,
and though it takes several more novels, Luke

00:02:11.141 --> 00:02:15.630
and Mara eventually fall in love and finally
get married in the 2000 Dark Horse comic Star

00:02:15.630 --> 00:02:16.660
Wars Union.

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:18.580
But that's not the end of their story.

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:23.420
Luke and Mara also have a son together named
Ben Skywalker, whose first name appears to

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:27.880
have been recycled in the sequel trilogy as
Ben Solo, aka Kylo Ren.

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:32.840
Ben Skywalker grows up to become an accomplished
Jedi like his mom, but Mara doesn't live to

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:33.340
see it.

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:37.960
She's murdered by her nephew, Jacen Solo,
while on his way to becoming Darth Caedus.

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:43.140
Mara Jade wasn't the only character of significance
to be introduced in Zahn's Thrawn trilogy.

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:48.330
There was also Luuke Skywalker, with two U's,
an evil clone who made his debut in the conclusive

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:50.500
novel in the trilogy, The Last Command.

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:55.720
In the story, it's revealed that the clone
was created by the mad Jedi Master Jorus C'baoth.

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:59.860
C'baoth made the clone using Luke's severed
hand that Darth Vader cut off during their

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:04.840
battle on Cloud City in The Empire Strikes
Back, and Luuke even wielded Luke's original

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:06.960
lightsaber that was also lost in that battle.

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:11.520
C'baoth sics Luuke on Luke, and the two engage
in an intense lightsaber duel.

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:15.300
Given that Luuke is a genetic clone of Luke,
and that he's received expert Jedi training

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:18.320
from C'baoth, the two are a perfect match
for each other.

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:23.460
Their fight ends when resident badass Mara
Jade intervenes, using Leia's lightsaber to

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:25.600
slay both Luuke and Joruus C'baoth.

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:30.690
The real Luke comes to view Luuke as the fulfillment
of the vision he had on Dagobah in The Empire

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:35.300
Strikes Back, where he duels someone he thinks
is Darth Vader, only to realize it was himself.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:39.540
Luuke Skywalker may not have featured heavily
in the Expanded Universe, but the idea of

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:43.500
an evil Luke clone whose creation came about
thanks to one of the most iconic scenes in

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:45.760
the franchise is undeniably awesome.

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:49.760
Not every Skywalker story in the Expanded
Universe revolved around Luke.

00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:54.280
Leia also got some love in the EU, and she
got to do some pretty cool stuff in books

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:57.180
and comics that her on-screen counterpart
could only dream of.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:04:01.560
And one of Leia's best stories that will never
make it to the big screen is the adventure

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:06.710
she took in Marvel Comics' Star Wars #73,
which was published roughly two months after

00:04:06.710 --> 00:04:09.260
the release of Return of the Jedi in 1983.

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:13.960
The story, dubbed "Lahsbane" after the planet
on which it takes place, picks up not long

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:15.220
after the Battle of Endor.

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:20.700
Leia, Luke, Lando, Chewbacca, R2-D2, and C-3PO
are all still hanging out together, though

00:04:20.701 --> 00:04:25.630
Han Solo had gone missing at the time, and
they've recently picked up a new ally: a pink-skinned,

00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:26.960
female thief named Dani.

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:31.430
The gang heads to the planet Lahsbane to search
for the flight record of a Rebel pilot who'd

00:04:31.430 --> 00:04:35.620
crashed there, and they learn the records
they need are located across a vast canyon.

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:39.480
Leia and Dani hatch a plan to secretly secure
the records themselves.

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:44.280
So under cover of night, the two women cross
the canyon...in a pair of hot air balloons.

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:49.720
Okay, yes, this story is ridiculous, but the
idea of Leia going on a female-only adventure

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:53.920
to prove her worth, even in a hot air balloon,
would've been fun to see on the silver screen.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:58.340
If there's one thing Star Wars desperately
needs, it's a Jedi pirate.

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:00.780
And that's exactly what Cade Skywalker is.

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:05.440
Debuting in Dark Horse's Star Wars: Legacy
comics, Cade's story takes place many years

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:08.240
after the exploits of our traditional Star
Wars heroes.

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:13.100
Over 100 years after, in fact, as Cade is
the great-great-grandson of Luke Skywalker.

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:18.020
And since canon Luke had no children, that
means we'll never see a Cade Skywalker movie,

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:19.000
and that's a shame.

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:22.420
Cade Skywalker is downright awesome, there's
no getting around it.

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:26.780
The guy is basically a cross between Luke
and Han, with a little Boba Fett and Jack

00:05:26.780 --> 00:05:28.520
Sparrow thrown in for good measure.

00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:31.840
"You are, without doubt, the worst pirate
I've ever heard of."

00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:34.260
"But you have heard of me."

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:39.320
He was raised a Jedi, but after seeing his
father murdered, he takes a different path

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:41.740
by operating in the seedier side of the galaxy.

00:05:42.030 --> 00:05:46.020
He becomes a pirate and a bounty hunter, and
he has his own sweet ship with a loyal crew

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:47.000
of scallywags.

00:05:47.390 --> 00:05:51.300
Cade eventually is confronted with his past
when he's discovered by the Sith Lord Darth

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:54.280
Krayt, who seeks him out due to his Skywalker
heritage.

00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:58.950
Cade ends up reluctantly embracing his Jedi
roots and proves to be an extremely powerful

00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:02.960
Force user, taking the fight to Krayt and
eventually killing him in combat.

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:07.400
Cade Skywalker's story is one of the EU's
most thrilling adventures, and it would give

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:10.440
Star Wars fans something they hadn't seen
in a movie before.

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:13.060
But alas, it seems like they never will.

